WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.176
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.476 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:15.240
Unit nineteen: Helping Others. Today you will talk about helping people using gerunds as subjects.

4
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.088
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.266
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:23.804
Help.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:27.199
Help means to make things easier for someone.

8
00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:29.760
I help my neighbor carry water.

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.840
Your turn. Say: Help.

10
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.318
Help.

11
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:38.096
Kindness.

12
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:41.965
Kindness means being friendly, caring and generous.

13
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.654
Small acts of kindness matter.

14
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.751
Your turn. Say: Kindness.

15
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.671
Kindness.

16
00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:53.232
Generous.

17
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:57.203
Generous means happy to give time, money or things.

18
00:00:57.817 --> 00:00:59.990
Our generous teacher buys us books.

19
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:03.201
Your turn. Say: Generous.

20
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.126
Generous.

21
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:09.140
Volunteer.

22
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:13.229
Volunteer means to work without pay to help others.

23
00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:16.432
I volunteer at the library on Saturdays.

24
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:19.646
Your turn. Say: Volunteer.

25
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.675
Volunteer.

26
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.302
Community.

27
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:29.001
Community means the people who live in one area.

28
00:01:29.617 --> 00:01:31.628
Our community built a new well.

29
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:34.741
Your turn. Say: Community.

30
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.729
Community.

31
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:40.252
Care.

32
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.702
Care means to feel that something is important.

33
00:01:44.317 --> 00:01:46.270
I care about elderly people.

34
00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:49.524
Your turn. Say: Care.

35
00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:53.182
Care.

36
00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:54.825
Support.

37
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:57.944
Support means help and encouragement.

38
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.143
Thank you for your support.

39
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.286
Your turn. Say: Support.

40
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.134
Support.

41
00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:08.757
Give.

42
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.715
Give means to let someone have something.

43
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:14.328
We give rice to families in need.

44
00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:17.174
Your turn. Say: Give.

45
00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:21.011
Give.

46
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:25.137
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:28.134
Visal, have you ever volunteered?

48
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.528
Yes. I teach English to younger kids in my village.

49
00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:35.804
How does it feel?

50
00:02:36.917 --> 00:02:40.556
Helping others feels great! Teaching kids makes me happy.

51
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.510
Why is volunteering important?

52
00:02:44.617 --> 00:02:48.242
Volunteering builds a strong community.

53
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.283
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.125
Grammar focus: Gerunds as subjects.

55
00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:56.658
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:59.071
Helping others feels good.

57
00:02:59.983 --> 00:03:02.169
Volunteering builds community.

58
00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:04.839
Giving makes people happy.

59
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:10.493
A gerund subject is singular, so the verb takes -s: Helping feels good.

60
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.541
Be careful! Don't say: Help others feels good.

61
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.045
Say: Helping others feels good.

62
00:03:19.345 --> 00:03:22.018
When a verb is the subject, use the -ing form.

63
00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:25.555
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.482
Small Acts, Big Difference.

65
00:03:28.782 --> 00:03:31.664
Helping others brings real kindness into the world.

66
00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.189
Being generous with your time shows that you care.

67
00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.604
Every Saturday, I volunteer at the community library.

68
00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.447
Reading stories to small children makes them smile.

69
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:48.174
Giving support, even in small ways, can make a big difference.

70
00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:53.350
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:54.183 --> 00:03:55.742
blank others feels good.

72
00:03:56.042 --> 00:03:59.393
A, Helping. B, Help. C, Helps.

73
00:04:02.933 --> 00:04:04.898
The answer is A: Helping.

74
00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.479
Being friendly, caring and generous is blank.

75
00:04:08.779 --> 00:04:12.386
A, kindness. B, community. C, support.

76
00:04:15.933 --> 00:04:18.003
The answer is A: kindness.

77
00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.695
To work without pay to help others is to blank.

78
00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:25.486
A, volunteer. B, give. C, care.

79
00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:31.660
The answer is A: volunteer.

80
00:04:32.867 --> 00:04:36.007
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:40.129
Describe a time you helped someone. How did it feel?

82
00:04:48.917 --> 00:04:50.394
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:50.694 --> 00:04:58.663
Last week, I helped an old woman carry her shopping. Helping her felt wonderful, and she gave me a big smile.

84
00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:00.545
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:05.681
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and gerunds as subjects.

86
00:05:05.981 --> 00:05:09.458
Today's value is kindness. Be kind to everyone.

87
00:05:09.758 --> 00:05:12.515
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

88
00:05:12.815 --> 00:05:15.548
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

